title: 'hrmp: return deposits of a confirmed request that cannot be enacted'
doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    A confirmed open channel request whose sender or recipient is no longer a valid para when it
    is enacted at a session change was dropped without giving back either deposit. This happens
    when either para deregisters in the session in which the request is accepted: the para is
    marked offboarding immediately but only becomes outgoing two sessions later, so the request
    cleanup for outgoing paras never sees it.

    Both deposits are now given back through the deposit provider, as when a channel is closed.

    No storage, API or configuration change. Deposits already left reserved by earlier versions
    are not touched.
crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: patch
